// n22 — a fixed-point literal carrying an exponent.
//
// CORBA 3.4 §7.2.6.5: `fixed_pt_literal` is digits, an optional point, more
// digits and a `d`. There is no exponent production, so `1e3d` is a floating
// literal wearing a suffix — omniidl 4.3.4 says "Cannot interpret floating
// point literal as fixed point" (measured 2026-08-21). Our lexer used to build
// the token by stripping the `d` and calling `f64::parse`, which accepted it
// and produced 1000.0: a value of the wrong type by a route that could not
// report anything, because the suffix had already been thrown away.
//
// **This file held the 31-digit case too, and never measured it** (2026-08-25).
// Lexing stops at the first failure and returns one error, so the second
// constant was never reached: the file was rejected for its first line and its
// header claimed two refusals it could not have shown. One lexical refusal per
// file, or the second one is a sentence rather than a measurement. The digit
// cap is n23.
//
// 지수부가 붙은 것은 fixed 리터럴이 아니다. 어휘 실패는 하나만 보고되므로
// 자릿수 상한은 n23으로 분리한다 — 한 파일에 두 개를 쓰면 두 번째는 측정이
// 아니라 문장이 된다.
module n22 {
  const fixed SCALED = 1e3d;
};
